y created + 1 duplicated/renamed), each independently editable, demonstrating management of multiple variations within the session.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Searching lowercase 'software' matched titles containing 'Software' (case-insensitive); Oldest First / Newest First sort correctly reordered results by creation date; clearing search restored all 5 resumes.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Date filter feature not implemented\", \"actual\": \"Dashboard only exposes a title search box and a sort dropdown (Newest/Oldest/Title A-Z/Title Z-A). No control exists to filter resumes by an exact creation date or a creation-date range (checked semantic_snapshot with includeHidden and full browser_snapshot - no date filter UI present).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No date validation for experience periods\", \"actual\": \"Setting End Date (2019-01) before Start Date (2020-01) was accepted silently - preview showed 'Jan 2020 – Jan 2019' with no error message and aria-invalid was null. Setting Start Date to a future month (2027-01, current date is Aug 2026) was also accepted without any rejection or feedback (preview showed 'Jan 2027 – Jun 2022').\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Experience/education start/end date inputs use type='month' (consistent MM/YYYY format shown as e.g. 'Jan 2020'). Checking 'I currently work here' cleared the end-date value and disabled the field (enabled:false); preview showed 'Jan 2020 – Present'. Unchecking re-enabled the field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No persistence across reload\", \"actual\": \"After reloading the app, all session changes were lost: the newly created resume ('Software Engineer Resume v2'), its duplicate/rename ('Software Engineer - Startup Application'), and the deletion of 'Marketing Manager Resume' were all reverted. Dashboard showed only the original 3 seed resumes (Product Designer Resume, Marketing Manager Resume, Software Engineer Resume) with their original data, as if no session changes had occurred.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Missing validation feedback for empty/whitespace title rename\", \"actual\": \"Entering a whitespace-only title and submitting correctly reverted the title to its previous non-empty value ('Software Engineer Resume v2'), but no toast, inline error, or any other validation message was shown to the user (checked notifications region and DOM for role=status/alert/toast elements - none present).\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing name, editing summary/experience/education/skills, and switching templates instantly updated preview.document content without any save/refresh action.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Section reorder (Education moved above Experience) and visibility toggle updated preview instantly; order persisted after navigating to Contact tab and back.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edits were preserved across tab navigation, dashboard return, and reopening; dashboard card showed 'Updated Aug 25, 2026' reflecting the recent edit.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Added 6 experience entries with content; all 6 rendered fully in preview.document DOM (no truncation), and full page/preview area became scrollable (docScrollHeight 2906 vs innerHeight 720) so entire resume remained readable via scrolling. All visible sections with content (contact, summary, experience, education, skills) rendered.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"After navigating tabs, returning to dashboard, and reopening the resume, all contact details, summary, experience, education, and skills remained present.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Edited copy's Full Name (unaffected original); then edited original's Location to 'Boston, MA' - copy's Location remained 'New York, NY' and its Full Name remained 'Jane Doe (Copy Edit)', confirming bidirectional independence.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed resume to 'Software Engineer Resume v2'; new title shown in editor.title and on the dashboard card after returning to dashboard.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Renamed Experience section heading to 'Career History' via Sections tab; heading appears with that customized text across Modern, Classic, and Minimal styles (with per-style casing).\"}]}"
